=== plain ===
\e[48;2;52;53;65m\e[0m
\e[48;2;52;53;65m show me how to count the go files\e[0m
\e[48;2;52;53;65m\e[0m
\e[3m\e[38;2;150;152;150mA loop over the listing is the shortest way to say it.\e[0m\e[0m

Try this.

\e[38;2;201;166;212mfor\e[0m \e[38;2;150;152;150mNAME\e[0m \e[38;2;150;152;150min\e[0m \e[38;2;201;166;212m$(\e[0m\e[38;2;150;152;150mls\e[0m \e[38;2;150;152;150m*.go\e[0m\e[38;2;201;166;212m)\e[0m; \e[38;2;201;166;212mdo\e[0m \e[38;2;240;198;116mecho\e[0m \e[38;2;181;189;104m"\e[0m$NAME\e[38;2;181;189;104m is quite a long line indeed\e[0m\e[38;2;181;189;104m"\e[0m; \e[38;2;201;166;212mdone\e[0m

That is all.

And a table, which changes shape as its rows arrive:

Tool\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0mWhat it does when it is asked to
read\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0mtakes a file and hands it back to you
grep\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0mwalks the whole tree looking for a pattern

That is the lot.

And a nested list, whose markers arrive before the items they introduce:

\e[38;2;192;128;80m• \e[0mread takes a file and hands it backand says how big it wasand leaves it where it found it
\e[38;2;192;128;80m• \e[0mgrep walks the tree for a pattern

That is the lot.

